            <ArticleTitle>Selective nerve root blocks for low back pain and radiculopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>243-56</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the management of patients with low back pain and radiculopathy, selective nerve root blocks (SNRBs) are now a common procedure for both diagnostic and therapeutic purposes. This article reviews the available studies as well as the relevant anatomy, pathology, technical considerations, and complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
